mation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to=
-node=3D"0">It=E2=80=99s a common point of confusion because of the names, =
but <b data-path-to-node=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"59">no, they are not e=
quivalent.</b> In fact, they solve two completely different performance pro=
blems.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">Think of it this way: the <b data-path=
-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"26">application property</b> is about =
how data is sent <i data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"73">to</i=
> the database (Writes), while the <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in=
-node=3D"109">annotation</b> is about how data is fetched <i data-path-to-n=
ode=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"149">from</i> the database (Reads).</p><hr =
data-path-to-node=3D"2"><h2 data-path-to-node=3D"3">1. The Property: <code =
data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"17">hibernate.jdbc.batch_size=
</code></h2><p data-path-to-node=3D"4">This setting controls <b data-path-t=
o-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"22">Write Optimization</b>.</p><p data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"5">By default, Hibernate sends SQL statements to the databas=
e one by one. If you save 100 users, Hibernate sends 100 separate <code dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-node=3D"123">INSERT</code> commands over=
 the network.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"6">When you set <code data-path-to=
-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"13">batch_size: 50</code>, Hibernate grou=
ps those statements together. It sends 50 inserts in a single network "trip=
."</p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"7"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0"><b dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Goal:</b> Reduce network =
round-trips during <code data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"=
40">SAVE</code>, <code data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"46=
">UPDATE</code>, or <code data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D=
"57">DELETE</code>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,1,0"><b data-path=
-to-node=3D"7,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Analogy:</b> Instead of driving=
 to the grocery store 50 times to buy 50 apples, you go once and bring a cr=
ate that holds 50.</p></li></ul><hr data-path-to-node=3D"8"><h2 data-path-t=
o-node=3D"9">2. The Annotation: <code data-path-to-node=3D"9" data-index-in=
-node=3D"19">@BatchSize</code></h2><p data-path-to-node=3D"10">This is used=
 for <b data-path-to-node=3D"10" data-index-in-node=3D"17">Read Optimizatio=
n</b> (specifically the "N+1 Problem").</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"11">If y=
ou have a <code data-path-to-node=3D"11" data-index-in-node=3D"14">Parent</=
code> entity with a <code data-path-to-node=3D"11" data-index-in-node=3D"35=
">List&lt;Child&gt;</code>, and you fetch 10 parents, calling <code data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"11" data-index-in-node=3D"82">parent.getChildren()</code> usu=
ally triggers 10 separate <code data-path-to-node=3D"11" data-index-in-node=
=3D"132">SELECT</code> queries (one for each parent).</p><p data-path-to-no=
de=3D"12">If you put <code data-path-to-node=3D"12" data-index-in-node=3D"1=
1">@BatchSize(size =3D 10)</code> on the <code data-path-to-node=3D"12" dat=
a-index-in-node=3D"40">children</code> collection, Hibernate will wait unti=
l you need the children, then fetch the children for <b data-path-to-node=
=3D"12" data-index-in-node=3D"138">all 10 parents</b> in a single query usi=
ng an <code data-path-to-node=3D"12" data-index-in-node=3D"180">IN</code> c=
lause.</p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"13"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"13,0,0">=
<b data-path-to-node=3D"13,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Goal:</b> Reduce n=
etwork round-trips during <code data-path-to-node=3D"13,0,0" data-index-in-=
node=3D"40">SELECT</code> (Lazy Loading).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"13,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"13,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Analog=
y:</b> If 10 people in an office want coffee, instead of each person walkin=
g to the breakroom separately, one person takes 10 cups and fills them all =
at once.</p></li></ul><hr data-path-to-node=3D"14"><h2 data-path-to-node=3D=
"15">Comparison Table</h2><div class=3D"horizontal-scroll-wrapper"><div cla=
