e=3D"17">Why isn't there a per-entity Write property?</h2><p data-path-to-n=
ode=3D"18">Hibernate groups statements by <b data-path-to-node=3D"18" data-=
index-in-node=3D"31">type</b> and <b data-path-to-node=3D"18" data-index-in=
-node=3D"40">table</b>. When you execute a transaction, Hibernate maintains=
 a "ActionQueue."</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"19">If Hibernate allowed diffe=
rent batch sizes per entity in the same session, it would make the flushing=
 logic incredibly fragmented. It would have to stop one batch, start anothe=
r, and keep track of dozens of different counters simultaneously, which wou=
ld actually hurt performance more than it helps.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=
=3D"20">Summary Checklist</h3><ul data-path-to-node=3D"21"><li><p data-path=
-to-node=3D"21,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"21,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0=
