"25">INSERT</code> statements in one JDBC batch.</p></li></ul><hr data-path=
-to-node=3D"7"><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"8">Common Pitfalls with Self-Refere=
ncing &amp; Batching</h3><ol start=3D"1" data-path-to-node=3D"9"><li><p dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"9,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"9,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"0">Circular References:</b> If you try to save a <code data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"9,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"42">Troop</code> that is its own commande=
r, or a circular chain (A -&gt; B -&gt; A), Hibernate might struggle to ord=
er the batch correctly, leading to a <code data-path-to-node=3D"9,0,0" data=
-index-in-node=3D"178">ConstraintViolationException</code>.</p></li><li><p =
data-path-to-node=3D"9,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"9,1,0" data-index-in-no=
de=3D"0">The "N+1" on the Tree:</b> Even if <b data-path-to-node=3D"9,1,0" =
